# netsurf: document keeps its members on Document.prototype; the engine's
# per-object private records (patch 278)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 277)
#
# In a browser the document's only own property is location (unforgeable);
# everything else is Document.prototype's (and Node's / EventTarget's).
# Here document carried 136 own members, the bridge's internals among them
# (__createElementNative, __getBody, _reg, __msCap, __msRegOnce, _listeners,
# __ms_ready_fired, _elements, ...). hsw reads Object.getOwnPropertyNames
# (document).
#
#  - macsurf_qjs.c: __vitaP(obj), installed first in
#    macsurf_qjs_setup_globals, gives the engine a private record per object
#    (a WeakMap; not enumerable); qjs_priv() is its C side. The document's
#    native hooks are set on its record, and every engine script that used
#    them (createElement / createTextNode / ... wrappers, the document event
#    registry, DOMContentLoaded / load readiness) reaches them through
#    __vitaP(document); the load path writes readyState there. The stub
#    document's never-filled _elements map is gone.
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: each public own member of document moves
#    to Document.prototype -- a method as it is, a value as a read-only
#    accessor over the document's record (domain settable, as in browsers),
#    an accessor as it is -- on every pass (the bridge installs its members
#    again when the real document arrives). A document it did not build reads
#    undefined, as before (none inherits Document.prototype today: the
#    scratch documents of createHTMLDocument / DOMParser are their own
#    objects, and keep their own members).
#
# Not changed: scratch documents' layout; their querySelector does not see
# nodes appended after creation (found here, older than this patch).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-document-shape.html (DOCSHAPE 6/6, Chromium 6/6;
# the build before fails 1 and 2).
